CM ZS6BKW Multiband Antenna
CM Developed by Greg Mew
CM Model runs with onec.exe
CE

SY	Freq=14.2				'Frequency in MHz
SY	HWM=1.35				' Half Wavelength Multiplier
SY	EL=HWM*(150/Freq)			' Length of Half Wavelength 1.35
SY	FPL=0.5					' Length of Feed Point element
SY	HAG=15					' Height Above Ground
SY	FM=0.62					' Feeder Multiplier
SY	FL=FM*(300/Freq)			' Length of Feeder 0.62
SY	FP=HAG-FL				' Height of Feed Point
'SY	FPX=(FL^2-(HAG-FP)^2)^0.5		' When HAG is less than FL use trigonomety to determine position in X didrection


GW	1	101	0	-EL	HAG	0	EL	HAG	0.0005
GW	2	3	0	-FPL	FP	0	FPL	FP	0.0005
	

GE -1

GN  	2       0    0    0      13.0     0.005  

TL	1	51	2	2	450	FL

EX	0	2	2	0	1000	0.0


FR	0	293	0	0	2	0.1	

RP 	0 	181 	1 	1000 	-90 	90 	1 	1	 
EN

'Even using the recommended 34-foot open-wire matching section, the designer
'states that an antenna tuner is necessary for all-band operation.  AO confirms
'some pretty wild input impedances.  The radiation pattern on each band is just
'what you would expect for a center-fed wire of this length:  Dipole-like on the
'lower bands, cloverleaf-shaped on the higher.  All in all, this popular antenna
'does not seem to possess any special properties, operating like any ordinary,
'random-length center-fed wire.

